query: UPDATE "conversation_turns" SET "outputText" = $1, "intent" = $2, "selectedAgent" = $3, "latency" = $4, "status" = $5 WHERE "id" = $6 -- PARAMETERS: ["{\"summary\":\"Yes, you can exercise, and it is highly beneficial for managing diabetes. However, you must follow certain safety guidelines.\",\"sections\":[{\"title\":\"Recommended Exercises\",\"bullets\":[\"Walking: Start with a brisk 30-minute walk daily.\",\"Yoga and Stretching: Helps improve flexibility and reduces stress.\",\"Strength Training: Light exercises 2 to 3 times a week help control blood sugar.\"]},{\"title\":\"Important Safety Tips\",\"bullets\":[\"Check your blood sugar before and after exercising.\",\"Always keep a fast-acting source of sugar, like glucose tablets or fruit juice, nearby in case your blood sugar drops too low.\",\"Stay hydrated by drinking water before, during, and after your workout.\",\"Wear comfortable, well-fitting footwear to protect your feet from injuries.\"]}],\"actions\":[{\"label\":\"Consult Doctor\",\"action\":\"Consult your doctor before starting any new vigorous exercise routine.\"}],\"patient_text\":\"Yes, you can exercise, and it is highly beneficial for managing diabetes. However, you must follow certain safety guidelines.\\n\\nRecommended Exercises\\n• Walking: Start with a brisk 30-minute walk daily.\\n• Yoga and Stretching: Helps improve flexibility and reduces stress.\\n• Strength Training: Light exercises 2 to 3 times a week help control blood sugar.\\n\\nImportant Safety Tips\\n• Check your blood sugar before and after exercising.\\n• Always keep a fast-acting source of sugar, like glucose tablets or fruit juice, nearby in case your blood sugar drops too low.\\n• Stay hydrated by drinking water before, during, and after your workout.\\n• Wear comfortable, well-fitting footwear to protect your feet from injuries.\",\"en\":\"Yes, you can exercise, and it is highly beneficial for managing diabetes. However, you must follow certain safety guidelines.\\n\\nRecommended Exercises\\n• Walking: Start with a brisk 30-minute walk daily.\\n• Yoga and Stretching: Helps improve flexibility and reduces stress.\\n• Strength Training: Light exercises 2 to 3 times a week help control blood sugar.\\n\\nImportant Safety Tips\\n• Check your blood sugar before and after exercising.\\n• Always keep a fast-acting source of sugar, like glucose tablets or fruit juice, nearby in case your blood sugar drops too low.\\n• Stay hydrated by drinking water before, during, and after your workout.\\n• Wear comfortable, well-fitting footwear to protect your feet from injuries.\",\"hi\":\"Yes, you can exercise, and it is highly beneficial for managing diabetes. However, you must follow certain safety guidelines.\\n\\nRecommended Exercises\\n• Walking: Start with a brisk 30-minute walk daily.\\n• Yoga and Stretching: Helps improve flexibility and reduces stress.\\n• Strength Training: Light exercises 2 to 3 times a week help control blood sugar.\\n\\nImportant Safety Tips\\n• Check your blood sugar before and after exercising.\\n• Always keep a fast-acting source of sugar, like glucose tablets or fruit juice, nearby in case your blood sugar drops too low.\\n• Stay hydrated by drinking water before, during, and after your workout.\\n• Wear comfortable, well-fitting footwear to protect your feet from injuries.\"}","GENERAL_HEALTH_QUERY","general-health-agent",9981,"COMPLETED","92238d84-ce3f-420a-bc75-b307dc1eecd6"]
